      "question_text": "Which statement applies the order of operations correctly?",
      "structure": "spot-the-error",
      "mastery": false,
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "$-4+2\\times 3=-4+(2\\times 3)$",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "$-4+2\\times 3=(-4+2)\\times 3$",
          "why": "Grouped the addition first, but $\\times$ has priority over $+$."
        },
        {
          "text": "$-40-20\\div(-5)=(-40-20)\\div(-5)$",
          "why": "Grouped the subtraction first, but $\\div$ has priority over $-$."
        }
      ],
      "solution_text": "$-4+2\\times 3$\n$=-4+(2\\times 3)$\n$=-4+6$\n$=2$\nThe multiplication is done before the addition, so the first statement is correct."
